 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Read the question",
   "text": "Which expression equals the Boltzmann constant \\( k \\)? (Option C prints \\( N_0 \\); the usual symbol is \\( N_A \\).)",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "Per mole to per molecule",
   "text": "\\( R \\) is energy per kelvin **per mole**. Dividing by the number of molecules in a mole gives the value **per molecule**.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "Compute",
   "text": "\\[ k = \\dfrac{R}{N_A} = \\dfrac{8.314}{6.02\\times10^{23}} = 1.38\\times10^{-23}\\ \\text{J K}^{-1} \\]",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "Answer: (B)",
   "text": "The key is (B). If \\( N_0 \\) in (C) is meant as the Avogadro number it has the same value as \\( N_A \\), and (C) would then be the same expression.",
   "actions": []
  }
 ],
